      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly tempting to jump to conclusions when your smart home devices behave unpredictably, but physical factors like poor insulation, overnight heating cycles, or cloud service updates are far more likely culprits than remote hacking. To log these events, I strongly recommend checking the \"Developer Mode\" or admin logs in your hub's main settings where you can view timestamps for state changes rather than trying to manually record them. Even if perfect technical proof isn't available, gathering detailed logs of specific times and HVAC settings will form a solid foundation for discussing suspicion with your professional astronomer.",
